Package: indri
Title: Scalable Additive Genetic Covariance Estimation
Version: 0.4.0
Authors@R:
    person(given = "Diogo",
           family = "Melo",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           email = "diogro@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-7603-0092"))
Description: Estimates the additive genetic covariance matrix of
    high-dimensional trait sets by fitting a multivariate animal model on many
    small trait subsets and reassembling the subset estimates into a single
    positive semi-definite matrix. The per-subset fit is a plugin, so the same
    estimator can run on a Bayesian sampler or on a REML engine. The
    assembled covariances then drive multi- and single-trait genome-wide
    association scans in a linear mixed model, with optional dominance
    effects, permutation p-values and genotype-by-environment tests with an
    environment-specific polygenic background.
